  "ROMAN_EMPEROR_CLUES": {
    "Augustus": "Great-nephew and adopted heir of Julius Caesar who ended the civil wars and became Rome's first emperor in 27 BC",
    "Tiberius": "Augustus's stepson and successor, who spent his last years ruling from the island of Capri",
    "Caligula": "Nicknamed \"Little Boots\" as a child among the legions; assassinated by his own Praetorian Guard in AD 41",
    "Claudius": "Scholarly, limping emperor found hiding by the Praetorians after Caligula's murder; ordered the conquest of Britain in AD 43",
    "Nero": "Last emperor of the Julio-Claudian dynasty; blamed the Christians for the Great Fire of Rome in AD 64",
    "Vespasian": "Won the Year of the Four Emperors, founded the Flavian dynasty, and began building the Colosseum",
    "Titus": "Captured Jerusalem as a general, then as emperor oversaw the Colosseum's opening and the aftermath of Vesuvius's eruption in AD 79",
    "Domitian": "Last of the Flavian emperors and younger brother of Titus; assassinated in AD 96 after an increasingly autocratic reign",
    "Trajan": "First emperor born outside Italy (in Hispania); conquered Dacia and presided over the empire's greatest territorial extent",
    "Hadrian": "Trajan's successor, a devoted admirer of Greek culture who ordered a great wall built across northern Britain",
    "Antoninus Pius": "Presided over an unusually peaceful 23-year reign, and was adopted by Hadrian on condition that he adopt Marcus Aurelius",
    "Marcus Aurelius": "Stoic \"philosopher-emperor\" who wrote the Meditations while campaigning on the Danube frontier",
    "Commodus": "Son of Marcus Aurelius who fought as a gladiator in the arena and was murdered in AD 192, ending the era of the \"Five Good Emperors\"",
    "Septimius Severus": "North African-born emperor who won the civil war of AD 193 and founded the Severan dynasty; died at York while campaigning in Britain",
    "Caracalla": "Granted Roman citizenship to nearly all free inhabitants of the empire in AD 212 and murdered his co-emperor brother Geta",
    "Elagabalus": "Teenage emperor from Syria, a priest of a sun god, whose scandalous reign ended in his murder at about age 18",
    "Aurelian": "Reunited the empire by defeating Zenobia's Palmyrene Empire and the Gallic Empire, and built the walls that still ring Rome",
    "Diocletian": "Formed the Tetrarchy to share rule among four men, launched the Great Persecution of Christians, and retired voluntarily in AD 305",
    "Constantine the Great": "Won the Battle of the Milvian Bridge in AD 312 and founded Constantinople as his new capital"
  },
